{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"_kritt_extractor_helper\":true,\"stub\":false,\"stub_explanation\":\"\",\"results\":[{\"flow_summary\":\"A nested invocation made while another nonReentrant Raffle operation is still executing is rejected before the release body runs. No proceeds are read, changed, or transferred.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:375 Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds - Permissionless external dispatch reaches the entrypoint and its nonReentrant modifier.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:69 ReentrancyGuard.nonReentrant - Runs the reentrancy check before dispatching the function body.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:88 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantBeforeView - Detects that the shared guard is already ENTERED.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:90 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantBeforeView - Reverts with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall; releaseSponsorProceeds never reads sponsorProceeds.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Revert with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall before executing the release body.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol\",\"flow_line\":90,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"There are no calldata arguments. The caller controls invocation timing and reaches this terminal action by invoking the entrypoint during an external callback from another guarded Raffle operation while the shared guard is ENTERED.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"This is the entrypoint's concurrency boundary. User-controlled callbacks can attempt the nested call, and the guard prevents any second payout execution from entering while another protected operation has transient state.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"A normal invocation made when no sponsor proceeds are currently claimable reverts without changing state, transferring tokens, or emitting the release event.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:375 Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds - A permissionless caller enters the nonReentrant release function.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:94 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantBefore - Confirms the guard is open and marks it ENTERED for this call.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:376 Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds - Loads the current sponsorProceeds value into amount.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:377 Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds - Detects amount == 0 and reverts with NoSponsorProceeds.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Revert with NoSponsorProceeds; no ERC-20 call or SponsorProceedsReleased event occurs.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":377,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"There are no calldata arguments. The caller-controlled input is release timing: calling before settlement, after a prior successful release, or otherwise while sponsorProceeds is zero reaches this revert.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"The zero-balance validation prevents empty or replayed releases and ensures the externally triggered function cannot report or attempt a payout when no sponsor liability exists.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"With nonzero proceeds, the function clears the liability optimistically but reverts if the fixed sponsor recipient is classified at execution time as same-factory protocol plumbing. The revert restores sponsorProceeds and prevents the transfer and event.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:375 Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds - A permissionless call passes the nonReentrant pre-check.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:376 Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds - Snapshots a nonzero sponsorProceeds amount.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:377 Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds - Passes the nonzero-proceeds validation.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:378 Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds - Sets sponsorProceeds to zero before the external token interaction.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:379 Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds - Loads the write-once configured sponsorRecipient.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:380 Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds - Dispatches the state-derived recipient and amount to _transferQuote.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:593 Raffle._isProtocolDestination - Compares the recipient against the raffle, factory, quote token, VRF wrapper, prize token, implementation, and registered raffles.\",\"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:42 RaffleFactory.raffleImplementation - The generated getter supplies the canonical implementation address for screening.\",\"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:54 RaffleFactory.isRaffle - For a code-bearing recipient, the generated getter reports whether it is a registered raffle.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:565 Raffle._transferQuote - A true destination check reverts with InvalidQuoteDestination, rolling back the earlier zeroing.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Revert with InvalidQuoteDestination and atomically restore sponsorProceeds; no quote tokens move.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":565,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"There are no calldata arguments. The caller controls when screening occurs; the checked values are the stored nonzero amount and fixed sponsorRecipient. This path is reachable if an initially acceptable address, such as a predicted code-less future clone address, is later deployed and registered as a raffle.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"The runtime destination screen is a sensitive payout boundary whose result can depend on the factory's evolving raffle registry even though sponsorRecipient itself never changes. Atomic rollback preserves the unpaid claim when the destination is rejected.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"A nonzero release whose recipient passes destination screening can still terminate at the canonical quote-token call if the ERC-20 rejects the transfer. The entire transaction rolls back, including the prior sponsorProceeds zeroing, and no release event is emitted.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:375 Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds - A permissionless call passes the nonReentrant pre-check.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:376 Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds - Loads a nonzero proceeds amount.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:378 Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds - Clears sponsorProceeds before interacting with the token.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:379 Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds - Loads sponsorRecipient as the transfer destination.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:380 Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds - Dispatches to _transferQuote.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:565 Raffle._transferQuote - The protocol-destination validation returns false, allowing delivery to proceed.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:566 Raffle._transferQuote - Calls SafeERC20.safeTransfer on the immutable quoteToken with recipient and amount.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/utils/SafeERC20.sol:33 SafeERC20.safeTransfer - Wraps the ERC-20 transfer and rejects an unsuccessful response.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/utils/SafeERC20.sol:184 SafeERC20._safeTransfer - Performs the low-level IERC20.transfer(recipient, amount) call.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/utils/SafeERC20.sol:189 SafeERC20._safeTransfer - Bubbles a token revert; a false or malformed nonempty response instead causes SafeERC20FailedOperation at line 35.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"The quote-token transfer reverts or SafeERC20 raises SafeERC20FailedOperation; all release state changes and token-side effects roll back.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/utils/SafeERC20.sol\",\"flow_line\":184,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"There are no calldata arguments. Caller-selected timing determines when the state-derived call quoteToken.transfer(sponsorRecipient, current sponsorProceeds) is attempted; operational token conditions such as a pause or blocklist can reject it.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"The ERC-20 call is the external asset-delivery trust boundary. SafeERC20 and transaction atomicity ensure a failed delivery cannot permanently clear the sponsor's recorded claim.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"When sponsorProceeds is nonzero, the recipient is accepted, and the quote-token transfer succeeds, any caller can release the complete stored amount to the fixed sponsorRecipient. The function leaves sponsorProceeds at zero, emits caller attribution, resets the guard, and returns the paid amount.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:375 Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds - Permissionless external dispatch enters the nonReentrant function; there is no caller-identity authorization check.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:94 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantBefore - Confirms the guard is open and marks the call ENTERED.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:376 Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds - Snapshots the complete current sponsorProceeds balance into amount.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:377 Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds - Requires the snapshot to be nonzero.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:378 Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds - Clears sponsorProceeds before the external interaction.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:379 Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds - Loads the write-once configured sponsorRecipient; msg.sender cannot select the recipient.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:380 Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds - Dispatches recipient and amount to _transferQuote.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:593 Raffle._isProtocolDestination - Screens the recipient against known same-factory protocol destinations and returns false.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:566 Raffle._transferQuote - SafeERC20 invokes quoteToken.transfer(sponsorRecipient, amount), which succeeds.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/utils/SafeERC20.sol:184 SafeERC20._safeTransfer - Executes the external ERC-20 transfer sink and accepts its successful response.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:381 Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds - Emits SponsorProceedsReleased(msg.sender, recipient, amount), attributing the trigger without paying the caller.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:102 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantAfter - Restores the guard to NOT_ENTERED before amount is returned.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Transfer the complete current sponsor-proceeds amount in quote tokens to sponsorRecipient, emit SponsorProceedsReleased, and return amount to the caller.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":566,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"There are no calldata arguments. The caller controls only execution timing and the msg.sender value recorded in the event. The sink arguments are state-derived: to = sponsorRecipient and value = the nonzero sponsorProceeds snapshot previously allocated during settlement.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"This is the sole successful asset-moving path. It is deliberately permissionless, but neither payout destination nor payout size is caller-selectable; effects-before-interactions, runtime destination screening, SafeERC20, and the reentrancy guard protect the transfer boundary.\"}]}"}}
